1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:16,528
The Valencia beach show happened this Sunday. Everything that exploded was scheduled to — in our line of work, that's called success. What's left is people: the crew to thank, the suppliers to restock, the inspector to reassure. Every one of them lives here.

2
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:37,659
This is everyone behind BoomClaw. A VP of Explosions. An HR manager whose handbook is on version twelve. An intern who is, on day thirty, surprisingly still alive. Tags cut the list to the people you need.

3
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:59,475
One click opens the whole story. Rodney Fizzlepop, head of R and D. Brilliant inventor — has lost his eyebrows four times this year. The company physician tracks their regrowth; that's in her card. Everything you'd normally keep in your head, written where the team can find it.

4
00:01:00,375 --> 00:01:16,226
And when a name escapes you, search what you remember instead. Chrysanthemum… and there's Yuki, the artist from the Japan collab. Her shells are pure art; the three a.m. video calls, apparently worth it. A note is enough to find a person.

5
00:01:19,375 --> 00:01:33,242
Now, from the chat. Ask the way you'd ask a colleague: who wires our shows? Francis searches the contacts and hands back the person as a chip — Dr. Sparky Voltman. Motto: if it sparks, I can tame it.

6
00:01:37,375 --> 00:01:49,322
New information goes the same way. The Baroness has a new phone number — and yes, she insists on Baroness; we comply. Say it, and the card is updated. No form, no digging.

7
00:01:54,375 --> 00:02:03,036
And the chip is the door. Click it, and you're standing on her card — new number saved, title intact, exactly where the crew will look for it.

8
00:02:10,375 --> 00:02:25,948
It's all one system. The supplier's card links the invoice from the show, even the sample inspection at the port — every thread of the story in one place. And we still owe Dragon Fireworks a reorder. That's next week's episode: Mail.

9
00:02:30,675 --> 00:02:37,822
That's Contacts — every person it takes to make things go boom, all on your own hardware. Next week: Mail.
